# KB maintenance with every launcher update

The user requires the KB Library to stay current with all future implemented
updates. Treat documentation maintenance as part of completing each update.

- Review each change for effects on installation, setup, app management, profiles,
  appearance, settings, platform support, performance, privacy and troubleshooting.
- Update relevant existing articles in `content/experience.json`. Add an article
  when a distinct new topic needs its own guide. Preserve existing `Launcher-KB`
  numbers and assign new numbers after the highest existing number; never reuse
  or renumber an existing reference.
- Keep `desktop/experience.json` identical to the shared content source so the
  Windows, macOS and Linux libraries stay aligned.
- Include relevant real screenshots wherever they help explain the instructions.
  Refresh affected captures when the interface changes. Use sanitized example
  data, never passwords, keys, tokens or private user content. Add or adjust the
  illustration mappings and captions in `tools/build-kb.py` as needed.
- Regenerate `docs/KB Library.docx` using `tools/build-kb.py` with the bundled
  workspace Python. Keep its release/date metadata accurate. Follow the documents
  skill when authoring or editing the Word artifact.
- Preserve clickable index entries, orange KB reference buttons and Back to index
  buttons. Ensure every link points to its corresponding article bookmark,
  including new KBs. Verify there are no unlinked references in document text.
- Render and visually inspect every page of the regenerated Word document before
  publishing. Check image readability, captions, page breaks and link destinations.
- Publish the updated articles, screenshots, generator changes and Word document
  with the relevant update on `TMApps-Launcher`. Keep the release attachment
  `KB.Library.docx` current when publishing a release.
- Describe only implemented and verified behaviour. Clearly label prepared or
  unavailable features and platform limitations. For changes with no user-facing
  KB impact, record that assessment instead of inventing an unrelated article.
